<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  The App Sandbox is deliberately off.

	  This app opens a vault file the user points it at, anywhere on disk, and
	  must reopen that same path on every launch. Under the sandbox that needs
	  security-scoped bookmarks in native Swift — real complexity for no gain
	  here, since the file the user chose is the whole point.

	  What the sandbox would otherwise buy is containment if this app were
	  compromised. That trade is the user's to make, and they make it knowingly:
	  the project ships as source, so whoever runs this compiled it themselves
	  from these entitlements. No signed binary is distributed.

	  Turn it back on before that changes — before shipping a build anyone else
	  runs, and certainly before the App Store, which requires it.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
